<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ site.language }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Redirecting… | {{ site.shortTitle }}</title>
  {%- comment -%}
    /about/ moved to /about-me/. This stub keeps any existing bookmarks/external links/search
    results pointing at the old URL from breaking — meta refresh handles browsers, the canonical
    tag and noindex tell search engines to update their index to the new URL instead of indexing
    this stub as its own page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/about-me/">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ '/about-me/' | toAbsoluteUrl }}">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
</head>
<body>
  <p>This page has moved to <a href="/about-me/">/about-me/</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
